  "about": "Screw thread sizes for Mitcad's hole and thread features. Mitcad's own data (MIT licence): the nominal diameters and pitches of the ISO metric general purpose series (ISO 261) and of the Unified series (ASME B1.1), of the Whitworth series (BSW, BSF; BS 84) and the parallel pipe threads G (ISO 228-1, their major diameters), and of the taper pipe threads NPT (ASME B1.20.1, the pipes' outside diameters), which are size designations only. Every other dimension is computed from the basic profile: ISO 68-1's 60-degree one for ISO metric and Unified threads, H = 0.866025 P, D1 = D - 1.082532 P, D2 = D - 0.649519 P; the 55-degree Whitworth one, h = 0.640327 P, D1 = D - 2 h, D2 = D - h; the taper pipe one, h = 0.8 P, D1 = D - 2 h, D2 = D - h (its 1:16 taper is not kept). Tolerance classes are labels; no tolerance values are listed.",
